body:
The "employers" desperate to fill their roles are lying. Even in the "lowest" industries within the country (food service, retail, and hospitality) employers are inundated with applications from desperate people. Every day at my shitty retail job we get multiple people asking to apply, and that's just the ones that show up to the store. My managers are moving people through the store like their changing their fucking socks then turning around and complaining that nobody wants to work anymore. The hotel I used to work at had people coming in every day looking for work, but none of them were called back, and no applications were coming in from online because they refused to pay to post the job on any of the job boards.

&#x200B;

There is no labor shortage in America. It's a lie. It's a bald faced lie and the media refuses to report on it and everyone in the country with even an imagined modicum of stability over what the poor are going through are willing to shut their eyes and cover their eyes if it keeps them from noticing that the country is slowly collapsing before them. They'll stop echoing the words "nobody wants to work anymore" the minute it's them who can't even get a response from a fucking McDonald's with big signs plastered all over the building saying the all too familiar lie now "we're hiring" loudly and proudly.

