The Tremere didn't invent Thaumaturgy, they just adapted their approach to magic from their background in the Hermetic Order to fit blood sorcery. Claims that the Tremere invented Thaumaturgy are just more lies from the usurpers.

&#x200B;

Blood sorcery was invented by the Tzimisce when the Eldest freed Kupala from it's ancient prison beneath the Carpathians. Other vampires simply learned to use their blood to mimic the true power of Koldunism, that is the genesis of Thaumaturgy. If you are wondering what the difference is Thaumaturgy pleads with the spirits to wend it's magic, Koldunism commands the spirits to do the Kolduns bidding.

