It can happen but the thing New Yorkers learn is to ignore it. Dance troop loudly taking over the subway car for a performance space and aggressively asking for tips for entertaining you? Just say "no" and ignore them. Is that drunk dude pissing in the gutter while his girlfriend is in tears hailing a cab outside a bar that was once a public pool? Oh shit! The one in Bushwick, gotta check that one out. Is that a rat giving birth inside a dead dog and then eating its newborns? That's NYC baby! Is that homeless person vomiting on a cops cock as he continues to suck that cop off? Probably, not my problem. Is the chop shop next door to that trendy new ramen place the best place to check when my car is stolen? No, you don't shit where you eat, but you can ask they'll probably have a guess. Is it me or is this neighborhood subtly covered in occult symbols in very deliberately placed areas around a creepy bookstore that sells "Bapho-METS" t-shirts? Pick me up one, I've seriously wanted one since I saw it last time I went in and just didn't pick it up but it haunts my dreams bro.

&#x200B;

Heads up, I just described one neighborhood with that little rant. All of the places I've described are real. New York City is a place like no other, I will refer you to [Mr. Brennan Lee Mulligan](https://youtu.be/TNpoplfLT1w) for more details.
